SUMMARY:Math — Practice make a ten to add & make a ten to subtract (no 
 new homework)
DESCRIPTION:Teacher: Sobia Yousufi\n\nNO new math homework sheet goes hom
 e Wednesday — this replaces it. Ms. Yousufi: “tomorrow I will not be
  sending home a new homework assignment. Instead\, I would like you to u
 se that time to practice these two skills with your child.” The post w
 ent out Tuesday 9/15 at 9:28pm\, so “tomorrow” is Wednesday 9/16 —
  she names the day\, so doOn is not a guess. Nothing is handed in\, so d
 ue is set equal to doOn. Use her exact class language and the ten frame 
 with counters\, not mental math: SUBTRACTION — “First is a circle\, 
 second is an X.” “Subtraction Man” starts at the smaller number (t
 hat is how many Xs)\, and drops counters on the ten frame until he reach
 es the bigger number. ADDITION is the opposite — “First is an X\, se
 cond is a circle” — then make a ten and add. She asks parents to wat
 ch and download her videos so home matches class\; the subtraction video
  is already posted and she says another video showing the addition proce
 ss is coming Wednesday. Her videos have not come through the ParentSquar
 e API before (see ps-88357074-video-review)\, so open the post in Parent
 Square directly to play them. Wednesday is the third day on subtraction\
 ; both skills are on Friday's quiz.\n\nOriginal post: https://www.parent
 square.com/feeds/88541895\nBoard: https://xwang12.github.io/wk-6d9fc5/\n
 Unofficial parent-made feed — confirm anything that matters with your 
 teacher.
